{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"USN-8801-1","published":"2026-09-22T10:17:44Z","modified":"2026-09-22T15:42:31.088486711Z","related":["UBUNTU-CVE-2025-10263","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-52938","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-53325","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-53361","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-53362"],"upstream":["CVE-2025-10263","CVE-2026-52938","CVE-2026-53325","CVE-2026-53361","CVE-2026-53362","UBUNTU-CVE-2025-10263","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-52938","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-53325","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-53361","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-53362"],"summary":"linux-azure-fde, linux-azure-fde-7.0 vulnerabilities","details":"It was discovered that some Arm processors could complete a broadcast\ntranslation lookaside buffer (TLB) invalidation before memory writes made\nthrough the invalidated translation were globally observed. A local\nattacker could possibly use this to write to memory after permission to do\nso had been revoked, bypassing memory protections or escalating privileges.\n(CVE-2025-10263)\n\nSeveral security issues were discovered in the Linux kernel.\nAn attacker could possibly use these to compromise the system.\nThis update corrects flaws in the following subsystems:\n  - Character device driver;\n  - Networking core;\n  - IPv6 networking;\n  - Unix domain sockets;\n(CVE-2026-52938, CVE-2026-53325, CVE-2026-53361, CVE-2026-53362)\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"linux-azure-fde-7.0","ecosystem":"Ubuntu:24.04:LTS","purl":"pkg:deb/ubuntu/linux-azure-fde-7.0?arch=source&distro=noble"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"7.0.0-1013.13~24.04.1"}]}],"versions":["7.0.0-1007.7~24.04.3"],"ecosystem_specific":{"availability":"No subscription required","binaries":[{"binary_name":"linux-azure-fde-7.0-cloud-tools-7.0.0-1013","binary_version":"7.0.0-1013.13~24.04.1"},{"binary_name":"linux-azure-fde-7.0-headers-7.0.0-1013","binary_version":"7.0.0-1013.13~24.04.1"},{"binary_name":"linux-azure-fde-7.0-tools-7.0.0-1013","binary_version":"7.0.0-1013.13~24.04.1"},{"binary_name":"linux-buildinfo-7.0.0-1013-azure-fde",